comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-07T17:45:24.101Z",codex-agent,"Related SDK evidence: this PR does not complete the CLI namespace consolidation, but it preserves package vocabulary in the SDK via PmClient.package and top-level packageLifecycle helpers while exposing package install/uninstall/doctor/manage/describe/reload/catalog/activate/deactivate/upgrade primitives. pm-tnud remains open because hidden alias shims, CLI full verb parity, contracts/MCP/completions regeneration, and install/upgrade alias specs are still outstanding."
  "2026-07-07T18:07:11.560Z",codex-agent,"Bundle note: SDK package lifecycle helpers now preserve package vocabulary in PmClient.package(...) even if caller options include a conflicting vocabulary value; this supports package namespace consistency while broader CLI namespace consolidation remains open."
  "2026-07-22T06:10:48.766Z",codex-root-20260722,"Dogfood finding from PR #643 (duplicate-safe reuse): unversioned pm install npm:pm-changelog --project preserved the existing managed 2026.7.18 package even after npm latest advanced to 2026.7.22, while a fresh CI checkout installed 2026.7.22. Explicit npm:pm-changelog@2026.7.22 upgraded correctly. The consolidated pm package install/upgrade surface should make current-versus-latest visible and give agents an explicit idempotent refresh path; this belongs to the existing pm-tnud lineage, not a duplicate item."
  "2026-08-26T18:50:49.501Z","harness:codex","TDD red evidence: package namespace grammar/help acceptance fails because extension, install, and upgrade remain visible and package lacks upgrade; focused run tests/integration/package-lifecycle-namespace.integration.spec.ts plus grammar contracts failed as expected before implementation."
  "2026-08-26T20:48:42.542Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence: repository lint passed end to end (ESLint, 0 jscpd clones, static quality, contracts, SDK/package parity, grammar 165/165, flag and refusal closure, graph composition, and record integrity over 54,662 history entries). Full sandboxed suite passed 584 files and 8,020 tests. Exact V8 coverage passed 100/100/100/100 with 59,625 statements, 44,867 branches, 12,396 functions, and 57,428 lines. Manual fresh-workspace acceptance installed pm-beads through 'pm package install', proved canonical/legacy upgrade stdout parity plus the deprecation hint, and activated the package successfully."
  "2026-08-26T21:10:15.978Z","harness:codex","Gate correction evidence: the final command-grammar gate exposed a hidden-alias modeling mismatch after the package namespace consolidation. Removed the hidden executable root 'extension' from the canonical destination census while retaining its deprecated alias contract and runtime behavior; updated the independent grammar-gate harness to hide deprecated top-level aliases from root help but recover their descendants from live command-summary seeds. Verification: node scripts/release/command-grammar-gate.mjs passed with 164 observed/164 declared commands and zero findings; focused grammar tests passed 20/20."
  "2026-08-26T23:41:58.008Z","harness:codex","Hosted exact-head remediation evidence: PR #1128 exposed two cross-surface gaps after the broad package namespace delivery. The SDK barrel now exports StructuredJsonValue for downstream package compilation; package upgrade is present in the runtime contract catalog; and package-first dogfood invokes the canonical nested command rather than relying on the hidden compatibility alias. Verification passed pnpm typecheck across root, type-tests, packages, and examples; 225 focused tests; 88 real package-first dogfood commands; full 584-file/8,025-test exact 100/100/100/100 coverage; and complete pnpm lint/static gates including generated contracts, defect evidence, graph quality, and append-only history."
